{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-logarithm","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:q-logarithm","kind":"definition","title":"$q$-Logarithm (categorical adjoint)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-exponential"],"tags":["hopf-algebra","primitive","q-logarithm","adjoint"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QLogarithm","text":"q-logarithm.md","leanSource":"q-logarithm.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:q-logarithm\"></a><p>A primitive of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{H}_q</code> satisfies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_q(p) = p \\otimes 1 + 1 \\otimes p</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\epsilon(p) = 0</code>. The <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-logarithm</strong> is the unique primitive <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\log_q \\in \\mathrm{Prim}(\\mathcal{H}_q)</code> satisfying</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\log_q \\circ \\exp_q \\;=\\; \\mathrm{id}.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm.md","heading":"Definition","number":"4.23.7","page":"b/def-q-logarithm","qa":{"counts":{"pass":80,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":67},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.QLogarithm","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-logarithm.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
